        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Teton County Idaho Search & Rescue – Emergency Communication</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/47045.webp" alt="Teton County Idaho Search & Rescue – Emergency Communication" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>$1,256.40 – Emergency Communication</p>

<p>Mountain communication is inconsistent, posing considerable risks to Search &amp; Rescue team members and those being rescued. The Community Foundation of Teton Valley chose to fully fund <a href="https://www.tcisar.org" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" aria-label="Teton County Idaho’s Search &amp; Rescue’s (opens in a new tab)">Teton County Idaho’s Search &amp; Rescue’s</a> competitive grant to strategically invest in four InReach locators. These GPS devices will be carried in the field by search teams to ensure another layer of communication and safety.</p>

<p>Communication with teams in the field, specifically in the mountains, is one of Search &amp; Rescue’s most difficult challenges when facing rescues.&nbsp;This problem has long plagued our local team, often leaving team members in the field with no contact to incident command.&nbsp;&nbsp;Search &amp; Rescue has tried to alleviate this issue by purchasing new, more powerful radios, utilizing mobile repeaters, including spending over $8,000 last year on a new mobile repeater.&nbsp;&nbsp;In the end, there have still been difficulties.&nbsp;&nbsp;<g>Command</g> is often left guessing where teams are and if they are safe.&nbsp;InReach emergency locators by Garmin will provide a more reliable means to track and communicate with team members. This will allow for safer searches and rescues within our community, as per Search &amp; Rescue’s mission to provide the public prompt, professional emergency services for people who are lost, injured, stranded, or in need of rescue, primarily within Teton <g>Couny</g>, Idaho.</p>
